{"cuisine/silesian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/silesian-cuisine","n":"Silesian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine"],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Poland","intro":[["Silesian cuisine belongs to the region of Silesia in Central Europe. It is a subtype of Polish cuisine with many similarities to and signs of the influence of neighbouring cuisines. The cuisine is particularly renowned for its poppy seed and knödel dishes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"silesian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silesian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine"],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Dishes","count":4,"links":[["Karminadle","dish/karminadle"],["Kluchy połom bite","dish/kluchy-po-om-bite"],["Potato salad","dish/potato-salad"],["Weißwurst","dish/wei-wurst"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine"],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/7f/0043_Gebratenes_Kaninchen%2C_2013.JPG/500px-0043_Gebratenes_Kaninchen%2C_2013.JPG","w":500,"h":344,"by":"Silar","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:0043_Gebratenes_Kaninchen%2C_2013.JPG"}},"ingredient/savoy-cabbage":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/savoy-cabbage","n":"Savoy cabbage","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Savoy cabbage (Brassica oleracea var. sabauda L. or Brassica oleracea Savoy Cabbage Group) is a variety or cultivar group of the plant species Brassica oleracea. Savoy cabbage is a winter vegetable and one of several cabbage varieties. It has crinkled, emerald green leaves,"]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-savoy-cabbage"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savoy_cabbage"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Irish cuisine","cuisine/irish-cuisine",[["Bacon and cabbage","dish/bacon-and-cabbage"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Cassoeula","dish/cassoeula"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Cut of pork","ingredient/cut-of-pork"],["Pig's trotter","ingredient/pig-s-trotter"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Pork ribs","ingredient/pork-ribs"],["Pork rind","ingredient/pork-rind"],["Tomato paste","ingredient/tomato-paste"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b9/Savoy_Cabbage.jpg/500px-Savoy_Cabbage.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Evelyn Gunn","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Savoy_Cabbage.jpg"}},"ingredient/custard":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/custard","n":"Custard","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 9 dishes across 7 cuisines","intro":[["Custard is a variety of culinary preparations based on sweetened milk, cheese, or cream cooked with egg or egg yolk to thicken it, and sometimes also flour, corn starch, or gelatin. Depending on the recipe, custard may vary in consistency from a thin pouring sauce (crème anglaise) to the thick pastry cream (crème pâtissière) used to fill éclairs. The most common custards are used in custard desserts or dessert sauces and typically include sugar and vanilla; however, savory custards are also found, e.g., in quiche."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-custard"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Custard"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":7,"groups":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Fraisier","dish/fraisier"],["Mille-feuille","dish/mille-feuille"],["Profiterole","dish/profiterole"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Fraisier","dish/fraisier"],["Mille-feuille","dish/mille-feuille"],["Profiterole","dish/profiterole"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Crostata","dish/crostata"],["Torta della nonna","dish/torta-della-nonna"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"]]],["Basque cuisine","cuisine/basque-cuisine",[["Pantxineta","dish/pantxineta"]]],["English cuisine","cuisine/english-cuisine",[["Manchester tart","dish/manchester-tart"]]],["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine",[["Wähe","dish/wahe"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Shortcrust pastry","ingredient/shortcrust-pastry"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Powdered sugar","ingredient/powdered-sugar"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Banana","ingredient/banana"],["Ladyfinger (cookie)","ingredient/ladyfinger-cookie"],["Vanilla Wafers","ingredient/vanilla-wafers"],["Jam","ingredient/jam"],["Nutella","ingredient/nutella"],["Ricotta","ingredient/ricotta"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/1f/Custard.jpg/500px-Custard.jpg","w":500,"h":458,"by":"No machine-readable author provided. Interiot~commonswiki assumed (based on copyright…","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Custard.jpg"}},"ingredient/sambal":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sambal","n":"Sambal","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 7 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Sambal is a category of chilli-based sauces or pastes originating in maritime Southeast Asia, particularly within the cuisines of Indonesia, Malaysia, Timor-Leste, Brunei, Singapore, southern Thailand and southern Philippines. Owing to historical connections and migration, sambal is also found in South Africa, Suriname and the Netherlands, while in Sri Lanka a local adaptation is known as sambol. In English, it is commonly described as an “Indonesian condiment” or “Malaysian condiment.”"]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sambal"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sambal"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Nasi kucing","dish/nasi-kucing"],["Plecing kangkung","dish/plecing-kangkung"],["Sate taichan","dish/sate-taichan"],["Udang balado","dish/udang-balado"]]],["Balinese cuisine","cuisine/balinese-cuisine",[["Plecing kangkung","dish/plecing-kangkung"]]],["Javanese cuisine","cuisine/javanese-cuisine",[["Nasi ambeng","dish/nasi-ambeng"]]],["Malay cuisine","cuisine/malay-cuisine",[["Nasi kerabu","dish/nasi-kerabu"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Turmeric","ingredient/turmeric"],["Shrimp paste","ingredient/shrimp-paste"],["Peanut sauce","ingredient/peanut-sauce"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Perkedel","ingredient/perkedel"],["Rempeyek","ingredient/rempeyek"],["Rendang","ingredient/rendang"],["Tempeh","ingredient/tempeh"],["Urap","ingredient/urap"],["Budu (sauce)","ingredient/budu-sauce"],["Clitoria ternatea","ingredient/clitoria-ternatea"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/c5/Sambal_cobek.JPG/500px-Sambal_cobek.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Midori","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sambal_cobek.JPG"}},"ingredient/tamarind":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/tamarind","n":"Tamarind","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 9 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Tamarind (Tamarindus indica) is a leguminous tree bearing edible fruit that is indigenous to tropical Africa and naturalized in Asia. The genus Tamarindus is monotypic, meaning that it contains only this species. It belongs to the family Fabaceae."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-tamarind"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamarind"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Konro","dish/konro"],["Lotek (food)","dish/lotek-food"],["Otak-otak","dish/otak-otak"],["Pempek","dish/pempek"],["Sate bandeng","dish/sate-bandeng"],["Sate klatak","dish/sate-klatak"]]],["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine",[["Panipuri","dish/panipuri"],["Pathia","dish/pathia"]]],["Palembang cuisine","cuisine/palembang-cuisine",[["Pempek","dish/pempek"]]],["Parsi cuisine","cuisine/parsi-cuisine",[["Pathia","dish/pathia"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Shallot","ingredient/shallot"],["Caraway seed","ingredient/caraway-seed"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Ipomoea aquatica","ingredient/ipomoea-aquatica"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Bird's eye chili","ingredient/bird-s-eye-chili"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Milkfish","ingredient/milkfish"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/2e/Tamarindus_indica_pods.JPG/500px-Tamarindus_indica_pods.JPG","w":500,"h":667,"by":"B.navez","lic":"CC BY 2.5","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tamarindus_indica_pods.JPG"}},"ingredient/gochu-garu":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/gochu-garu","n":"Gochu-garu","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Korean chili peppers or Korean hot peppers, also known as Korean red, Korean dark green, or Korean long green peppers according to color (ripening stages), are medium-sized chili peppers of the species Capsicum annuum. The chili pepper is long, slender and mild in flavor and spice. Green (unripe) chili peppers measure around 1,500 Scoville heat units."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-gochu-garu"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gochu-garu"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine",[["Gochujang","dish/gochujang"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili powder","ingredient/chili-powder"],["Glutinous rice","ingredient/glutinous-rice"],["Malt","ingredient/malt"],["Meju","ingredient/meju"]]}]},"ingredient/ham-hock":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/ham-hock","n":"Ham hock","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A ham hock (or hough) or pork knuckle is the joint between the tibia/fibula and the metatarsals of the foot of a pig, where the foot was attached to the leg. It is the portion of the leg that is neither part of the ham proper nor the ankle or foot (trotter), but rather the extreme shank end of the leg bone."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-ham-hock"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ham_hock"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine",[["Jokbal","dish/jokbal"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Pig's trotter","ingredient/pig-s-trotter"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b7/Schwein-Eisbein.png/500px-Schwein-Eisbein.png","w":500,"h":231,"by":"Rainer Zenz","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schwein-Eisbein.png"}},"ingredient/espelette-pepper":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/espelette-pepper","n":"Espelette pepper","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 3 cuisines","intro":[["The Espelette pepper is a variety of Capsicum annuum that is cultivated in the French commune of Espelette, Pyrénées-Atlantiques, traditionally the northern territory of the Basque people. On 1 June 2000, it was classified as an AOC product and was confirmed as a PDO (French: AOP, Appellation d'origine protégée) product on 22 August 2002.  Its flavor is described as sweet, fruity, and berry-like with a mild heat."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-espelette-pepper"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espelette_pepper"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Basque cuisine","cuisine/basque-cuisine",[["Piperade","dish/piperade"]]],["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Piperade","dish/piperade"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Piperade","dish/piperade"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bell pepper","ingredient/bell-pepper"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/58/France-Piment_d%27Espelette-2005-08-05.jpg/500px-France-Piment_d%27Espelette-2005-08-05.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Unknown author","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:France-Piment_d'Espelette-2005-08-05.jpg"}},"ingredient/hominy":{"t"